# Codex review posted 3 findings on PR #3173, all confirmed real:
#   P1: /tts-pcm-diagnostic is optionalAuth + no rate limit -- unauthenticated
#       billing/DoS vector against real Polly synthesis (up to 3000 chars/call).
#   P2: route-level normalizeLang() (orb-live.ts's live-session allowlist
#       version) silently maps any unsupported language to 'en' BEFORE the
#       route's own unsupported-language check can run -- a typo'd or
#       newly-Polly-supported lang gets a false 200 with English audio
#       instead of the intended 422.
#   P2: verify-cascade-audio-timing.ts only exercised the extracted
#       _pcmRateFromMime() parser -- a regression to
#       createBuffer(..., 24000) in the widget's real playback call site
#       would leave the parser untouched and every check would still pass,
#       silently missing the exact VTID-03711 defect this program exists
#       to catch.
#
# Fixes:
#   - Added a dedicated express-rate-limit limiter (20 req/15min), same
#     pattern as routes/live.ts's existing per-route limiters.
#   - Route now uses polly.ts's own normalizeLang (shape-only: lowercase,
#     strip region, NO allowlist-to-'en' fallback) instead of orb-live.ts's
#     live-session version, so synthesizePolly's own voice table/
#     POLLY_UNSUPPORTED_LANGS makes the real call.
#   - Added verifyWidgetWiringIsConnected() to the test program: a
#     structural check (run first, fatal on failure) proving createBuffer()
#     is wired to the variable _pcmRateFromMime() actually assigns, not a
#     hardcoded literal. Exported it (+ guarded the script's auto-run
#     behind require.main===module) so it has direct unit test coverage,
#     including a mutation test that reproduces the VTID-03711 defect
#     exactly and confirms the check catches it.

cd services/gateway
npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> clean, no output (outputs/tsc.txt)

npx jest test/orb/live/characterization/tts-pcm-diagnostic-route.characterization.test.ts --silent
#   -> Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total
#   -> Tests: 11 passed, 11 total (8 original + 3 for the Codex fixes)
#   -> outputs/targeted-tests.txt

npx jest test/scripts/verify-cascade-audio-timing.test.ts --silent
#   -> Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total
#   -> Tests: 4 passed, 4 total
#   -> outputs/verify-script-unit-tests.txt

npx jest test/orb --silent
#   -> Test Suites: 177 passed, 177 total
#   -> Tests: 6 todo, 3281 passed, 3287 total
#   -> outputs/full-orb-suite.txt

npx jest test/scripts --silent
#   -> Test Suites: 4 passed, 4 total
#   -> Tests: 60 passed, 60 total (includes the 3 pre-existing scripts/ suites)

